WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.663
- Oh Wyatt's cranky.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.083
(crying)

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.423
You're not hungry?

00:00:07.001 --> 00:00:10.861
Okay (laughs) you don't have to eat.

00:00:10.861 --> 00:00:13.444
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.263
^Hi I'm Hannah and I'm the world's okay-est mom.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.373
Now ever since I had my second kid,

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.880
I feel like date nights have totally gone out the window

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.580
but at this point he's three years old

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.740
so I've no excuse,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.190
it's time to bring them back.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.670
But I get that guilt of a working parent

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.580
where I'm gone five days a week

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.970
and leaving my kids for longer than I already do

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.963
just makes me feel super guilty.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:38.250
And plus if I had to plan a date night

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.460
I wouldn't even know where to start.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.530
So I want to try something

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.630
that I think will be fun for the whole family.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.440
I'm gonna let my kids plan my date night

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.653
start to finish.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.580
It could be four hours of just straight playing Legos

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.500
or it could actually be something really fun.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.980
As long as it's not watching Caillou, I'm cool with it,

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.330
so let's see what they say.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:58.363
I don't think my kids quite know what a date actually is.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.510
^I think Jackson's idea of a date

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.140
^comes from Disney movies

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.620
and in those,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.800
the date consists of the woman

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.400
dressing up in a ball gown

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.170
and there's magic and sparkles

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.700
and some fairy godmother blesses her with a wand

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.540
to make everything come to life.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.090
It's very over the top.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.640
^Wyatt's idea of a date is probably like a sword fight

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.120
^or something, he doesn't know anything (laughs)

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.863
^Have you guys given any thought to our date night?

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.153
- [Wyatt] No.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.180
- What do you think?

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.390
- First you go to Chuck E. Cheese

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:30.793
^- Chuck E. Cheese.

00:01:30.793 --> 00:01:32.363
^- Then you go to the park,

00:01:32.363 --> 00:01:33.963
^then you get ice cream,

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.653
^then you watch Adventure Time.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:37.953
^- All of that?

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.513
- [Wyatt] Yeah.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.547
- Oh my gosh, what do I wear to something like this?

00:01:43.547 --> 00:01:45.100
- [Wyatt] There's a lot of games.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.100
- There are a lot of games to play, huh?

00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:49.353
- There are a lot of toys.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.653
- A lot of toys?

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.593
Is Chuck E. Cheese dinner?

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:54.395
- Ice cream is dinner.

00:01:54.395 --> 00:01:55.540
- Ice cream is dinner too?

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.020
So Jackson made this little joke

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.000
about how we should have ice cream for dinner

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.833
on the date.

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:02.650
And Wyatt clearly was half listening the whole time

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.250
but then heard that little end bit

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.270
^and jumped in to remind us all

00:02:06.475 --> 00:02:08.306
^- [Wyatt] Ice cream is dessert.

00:02:08.306 --> 00:02:10.389
- No ice cream is dinner!

00:02:10.786 --> 00:02:11.619
^- [Wyatt] No it's not!

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.370
- Definitely not pleased with that idea

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.123
^and it was not going to happen.

00:02:16.392 --> 00:02:17.477
^- It's not dinner.

00:02:17.477 --> 00:02:18.683
- You're right.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.003
You guys, that's what you've decided?

00:02:21.752 --> 00:02:23.463
That's what we're gonna do.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.400
- But you need to dress up really fancy

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.793
fancy because it's a fancy date.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.340
- [Hannah] If you had a girlfriend

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.940
would you take her to Chuck E. Cheese?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.699
- Uh yeah.

00:02:33.699 --> 00:02:35.240
- Yeah? (laughs)

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.060
^I have my collagen eye pads on right now

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.560
so you know I'm taking this very seriously.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.890
Now when I went to get dressed for this date

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.680
I really had to reach back in the closet,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.280
kind of like behind all my daily wear

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.720
to bring out something that's a little fancy,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.460
up to Jackson's standards.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:57.620
As a mother, I feel like I shop very practically.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.940
Everything I buy is machine washable

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.910
because it's all gonna end up stained.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.340
I don't own cocktail dresses

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.610
or night time outfits

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.920
because whenever I go to buy one

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.364
I have to remind myself

00:03:09.364 --> 00:03:11.683
that I have no where to wear it.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.503
But for this, we're going out,

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.603
got a nice dress and I put in some effort.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.743
I got it together and got makeup on.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.583
Ready to go.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.643
^Matt looks very nice.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.803
He's very excited.
- [Matt] Excited.

00:03:26.237 --> 00:03:27.320
- Not at all.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:30.850
We realized that we kind of have to do things out of order

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.770
because if we go to Chuck E. Cheese and then the park

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.220
it's gonna be pitch black by the time we get to the park

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.720
and that means it's technically closed, I think,

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.023
they close at sun down.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.950
So we're gonna go to the park first,

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.363
then Chuck E. Cheese, then ice cream,

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.893
and then we're gonna watch Adventure Time.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.483
There's a free swing, but they're not next to each other.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.070
This is so embarrassing,

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.673
this park is full of kids.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.080
So our first stop was the park

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.730
which was the stop I was least excited for,

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.790
but we did it, we wanted to make good

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.700
on this date.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.430
Matt and I went and we forced ourselves to play

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.530
on the play equipment.

00:04:10.071 --> 00:04:11.443
(laughs) He's pushing me.

00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:16.496
Oh my God, we are so weird.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.553
He's pumping, he's into it. (laughs)

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.130
We made sure to go on each and every

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.120
piece of equipment

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.380
because I though that that constituted

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.863
a full park play experience.

00:04:30.644 --> 00:04:31.693
(screams) Oh my God!

00:04:33.198 --> 00:04:35.350
It never dawned on me until I actually went

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.740
and tried playing on this play equipment

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.710
that kids are a lot more dexterous than adults

00:04:41.425 --> 00:04:43.780
and I felt most embarrassed about the fact

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.180
that I could barely get through the monkey bars.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.727
I can't do that (laughs)

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.483
I can't do it, I'm weak.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.183
It's hard, it's hard to do!

00:04:54.783 --> 00:04:57.450
(playful music)

00:05:01.047 --> 00:05:02.297
I'm a dinosaur.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:06.420
One, two, three (yells and laughs)

00:05:06.678 --> 00:05:07.511
Oh my God.

00:05:07.511 --> 00:05:08.344
All aboard.

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.603
Matt's driving the train.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.020
Okay, this is so awkward

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.420
and I honestly wouldn't be surprised

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.700
if a parent approached us

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.220
and asked us to leave.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.053
We really stick out right now,

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.233
and also this park is so crowded.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.313
- We're getting a lot of looks.

00:05:24.313 --> 00:05:25.340
- We're getting a lot of weird looks,

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.240
so we're gonna go.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:29.210
This was fun.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.180
While at the park,

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.600
my first priority was just to not make eye contact

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.433
with anyone

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.770
or look at any child for too long.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.270
We had a couple fun moments,

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.390
it was all around very awkward,

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:42.603
but it wasn't horrible.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.930
So off to Chuck E. Cheese,

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.580
'cause that's not awkward either.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.853
Hey, oh it's bright.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:55.930
It's like early bird special dinner at Chuck E. Cheese.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.150
I don't even remember what kind of food they serve there,

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.963
I think they have pizza,

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:02.570
salad

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.172
- [Matt] Boxed wine.

00:06:04.172 --> 00:06:06.122
- Boxed wine.
- [Matt] That's what I'm

00:06:06.207 --> 00:06:07.287
excited about.

00:06:07.287 --> 00:06:09.483
- That's for sure necessary.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:13.479
I was so hurt and disappointed to find

00:06:13.479 --> 00:06:16.663
that they eliminated the box wine on tap.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.250
The last time I went to Chuck E. Cheese

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.840
they had boxed wine on tap,

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.693
that was actually my first legal drink,

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.603
was boxed wine on tap at Chuck E. Cheese.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.920
When did that happen?

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.423
I didn't see a press release.

00:06:30.361 --> 00:06:31.801
- [Matt] Ah, it ripped.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.279
- Mine too, cheers.

00:06:33.279 --> 00:06:35.273
Cheers guys!

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.920
So I was a little salty about it when I first

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:38.853
tried the wine.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:43.933
Devastating.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.913
Okay so we got wings,

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:51.370
endless salad bar, two glasses of wine,

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:55.210
a play pass, it was like 50 bucks, not bad.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:56.620
Such a mad house here

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:59.490
that literally nobody is noticing

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.890
that we don't have any kids

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.280
because it's full of parents sitting at the tables

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.173
by themselves while their kids play.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:09.303
So I'm kind of breathing a sigh of relief right now.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:11.963
I almost finished my wine already.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.703
23 tickets for taking a survey.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.450
We're gonna play this Batman whack a mole.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.423
I need a beer, okay.

00:07:20.616 --> 00:07:22.980
It didn't quite dawn on me

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:23.900
until we got there

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.680
how much Chuck E. Cheese is without kids.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.170
Usually when we go with the kids

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.410
they're playing all the games

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.470
and I'm just kind of there supervising,

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.670
eating some pizza.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.140
When we went without the kids,

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:35.820
we got to play everything.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.103
And I was there holding a beer in one hand,

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:40.083
playing Batman whack a mole,

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.813
just living my best life at Chuck E. Cheese.

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:52.034
(yelping on game)

00:07:54.404 --> 00:07:56.520
I am inherently competitive

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.410
and when it's me and Matt, I have to win.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.560
And so the most frustrating part about being at

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:02.490
Chuck E. Cheese with him

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:05.183
is that he was way better at the games than I was.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.773
Oh my gosh, you won 50 tickets

00:08:11.435 --> 00:08:14.435
- [Matt] Yeah!
- How did that happen?

00:08:14.911 --> 00:08:18.661
I'm genuinely excited, look at that, balling.

00:08:24.485 --> 00:08:25.318
That's it?

00:08:30.494 --> 00:08:31.744
Look at him go.

00:08:32.656 --> 00:08:34.183
It's Michael Jordan.

00:08:34.183 --> 00:08:35.423
Because I was losing,

00:08:35.423 --> 00:08:38.590
he was getting a multitude of tickets,

00:08:38.848 --> 00:08:40.485
and I'd had a little wine.

00:08:40.485 --> 00:08:42.376
I did a couple of things

00:08:42.376 --> 00:08:44.209
that I'm not proud of.

00:08:48.077 --> 00:08:49.538
- [Matt] Oh my God, are you stealing?

00:08:49.538 --> 00:08:51.590
Are you taking that ticket?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:52.423
So mean.

00:08:53.102 --> 00:08:54.810
- Nobody even wanted it.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.780
It was fair game, I'm sorry,

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:59.190
if you leave your tickets at the game,

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.656
that's just Chuck E. Cheese code of conduct

00:09:01.656 --> 00:09:03.380
rule number six.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.983
Thou hast left a ticket,

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:08.483
it shall be claimed by the nearest adult.

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.263
We've almost 200 tickets.

00:09:11.702 --> 00:09:12.887
I feel like that's pretty good.

00:09:12.887 --> 00:09:14.520
Matt and I got super excited at the end

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.680
when we were picking our prizes,

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.920
and you know we wanted to bring something back

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:18.753
for the kids.

00:09:18.753 --> 00:09:20.010
We were excited about picking out

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.350
something really cool for them.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.003
I'm gonna pass out right now.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.900
Can we get two of those rockets?

00:09:25.615 --> 00:09:27.024
- [Attendant] Two rockets.

00:09:27.024 --> 00:09:28.691
- Thank you so much!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.520
It was fun, and it probably was

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.110
partially due to the chardonnay,

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.823
but it was still fun.

00:09:36.631 --> 00:09:37.630
(laughs) I didn't really think

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:38.880
I'd be so into this.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.960
I'm so excited, we got a ball,

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:42.090
we're gonna give these to the kids,

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.140
we're not keeping them.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.640
- They're gonna be so psyched.

00:09:44.873 --> 00:09:46.970
- We got two rockets, Chuck E. Cheese rockets,

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.813
two balls and two spinning tops.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.230
Oh my gosh the boys are gonna be so excited

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.040
because they weren't expecting this.

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:57.253
I had the best time ever.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.763
I had the best time ever.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.260
Now after Chuck E. Cheese,

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.840
all that was left of the kid's date idea

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:06.350
was ice cream and Adventure Time, but

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:11.183
It's 6:30 p.m. (laughs) how you feeling?

00:10:11.604 --> 00:10:12.437
- I'm feeling good.

00:10:12.437 --> 00:10:14.560
- So we decided to go a little rogue

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.883
and incorporate a couple of grown up things.

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:21.173
Because I was dressed, I had makeup on,

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.220
we gotta do some more.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.100
We were not driving at this point,

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.280
we left the car at the house

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:30.710
and we took a ride share to all of these stops.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:32.543
We were not being irresponsible.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:34.143
We're parents, come on.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.767
Okay so we took a little detour.

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:41.513
When I've had a couple glasses of wine I like to shop.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.163
What they don't know won't hurt them.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:48.510
We're just expanding on our date.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:51.870
So while we were at the vintage store,

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:55.390
I just got completely caught up in this night for us

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.223
and we're out,

00:10:56.223 --> 00:10:58.150
and oh my gosh I'm gonna do this forever,

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.400
we're gonna do this every weekend.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.730
So I ended up leaving with this fake fur leopard coat

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.433
(laughs)

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:11.873
I'm so excited, this is what I got.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:16.290
Yeah, for future dates (laughs)

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:18.450
Okay so we're walking down the street,

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.000
this guy comes up to us and is like,

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.243
do you wanna go to a speak easy?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.540
And he's in front of this dark door,

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.730
and we say, well Matt says no,

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.573
and I say maybe.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.303
- I didn't say no, I just kept walking.

00:11:30.303 --> 00:11:31.137
- You just kept walking (Matt laughs)

00:11:31.137 --> 00:11:33.519
and I was down for it.
- [Matt] He was kind of creepy

00:11:33.519 --> 00:11:35.460
- I'm in this fur coat, so we ended up

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.790
getting into this speak easy.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.223
It's really cute.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.143
We got some mint juleps.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.103
- Cheers.

00:11:41.581 --> 00:11:43.460
- I mean date night has gone off the rails.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.300
At the speak easy we were able to just sit

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.343
in a quiet corner and people watch.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:53.590
I think it's a lot more of our vibe as adult parents,

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:56.970
we're not super I want to jump up and down for two hours.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:59.693
You just kind of want to sit and relax.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.010
Have a little cocktail.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:04.563
Last stop of an epic night, it's ice cream time.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.003
I'm a little over dressed.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.800
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.863
And finally at the end of the night,

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:17.590
we got home, put on Adventure Time,

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.713
and within 30 seconds Matt was passed out completely.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.210
That is a skill that I swear you get

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.043
when you're a parent.

00:12:25.043 --> 00:12:27.110
You can just fall asleep anywhere in 30 seconds.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:29.020
I mean I've seen Matt just fall asleep

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.800
with a coffee cup in his hand

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.403
because he needs to.

00:12:33.517 --> 00:12:36.453
Too much partying. (laughs)

00:12:40.391 --> 00:12:42.150
I'm not mad at him, I'm right there with him.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.200
I was like, I'm gonna film this

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.283
^and then pass right out myself.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.763
^I had a lot of fun on our date.

00:12:50.101 --> 00:12:51.110
- You like it?

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.643
- Yes, thank you for planning it.

00:12:54.228 --> 00:12:55.061
- You're welcome.

00:12:55.061 --> 00:12:56.290
- It was really fun.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.980
I wanna go back to Chuck E. Cheese more,

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.113
does that sound good?

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:00.533
- Yeah!

00:13:02.038 --> 00:13:03.240
- In the end, after this date,

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.140
I'm really grateful that I gave my kids the opportunity

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:06.973
to do this.

00:13:06.973 --> 00:13:08.530
I had a blast

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:10.640
and it just opened my mind

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.690
to a whole new perspective of what date night could be.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.323
Now what did I learn?

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:16.440
I learned a few things.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.770
I learned first that Matt and I

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:21.690
^can afford to go out a little bit more often.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.390
I feel like as parents,

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:26.170
the focus is so much on the kids all the time

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:29.210
that you lose that connection to each other sometimes

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:32.190
and you forget to take time for your partner.

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.850
So having the date night out of the house

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.860
and just doing something that was for us

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.360
really reminded me that I need to do more of it.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.200
^The second thing I learned was

00:13:43.094 --> 00:13:44.920
^I have a lot more energy than I thought I did.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.890
I think being a homebody,

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:51.090
it's the effort of motivating myself to go do something

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:52.550
that's most of the work,

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:53.960
and then once I'm out,

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.390
I'm there and I'm having fun

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.623
and I have energy.

00:13:56.961 --> 00:14:00.603
We just ended up going all night, and it was awesome.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.840
And then third, I'm not even ashamed to say

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:04.033
^that since that date,

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.580
^we've gone back to Chuck E. Cheese

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.100
^at least three times.

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:09.480
This is going to be a regular thing

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.973
for us and the kids.

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.470
It is so much fun

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.670
and I really think that at the end of the day

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.230
this date plan was Jackson's long con

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:18.880
to get to go to Chuck E. Cheese more.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.023
And it worked.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:21.720
So that's all I got for today.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:23.770
I'm Hannah, and if you have any date ideas,

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:24.690
^leave them in the comments

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.350
^or you can text me, this is a real number,

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.800
^I don't always respond 'cause I get a lot of messages,

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:29.963
^but I do read them all.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.713
If you'll please excuse us,

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:33.680
we're off to an epic date night

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.660
at Jackson's elementary school

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.000
at family dance night.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.450
Can you tell me any date ideas?

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:40.480
Please help us.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.603
Til next time.

00:14:42.829 --> 00:14:45.412
(upbeat music)

00:14:46.524 --> 00:14:47.624
Are you ready to rage?

00:14:49.782 --> 00:14:51.675
(laughs)

00:14:51.675 --> 00:14:54.258
^(upbeat music)

